# CODEOWNERS — coverage model (un-inverted).
#
# DEFAULT = UNOWNED: any path not matched below needs no code-owner review, so a
# low-risk deterministic PR (and a Margot LOW-risk verdict) can merge without the
# operator. There is deliberately NO `* @owner` catch-all.
#
# OWNED (listed below) = paths where a JUDGMENT change must have a human: the
# safety / identity / gate machinery. The branch ruleset requires code-owner
# review (with 0 baseline approvals), so touching any owned path holds the PR for
# @lexijamesesq; touching only unowned paths does not.
#
# When adding a path: uncertain -> OWNED (under-coverage — an owned path left
# unowned — is the dangerous direction). Here the owned surface is the
# command-execution / trust boundary; the declarative HA content is the flow lane.

# --- Gate machinery (CI) ---
/.github/workflows/            @lexijamesesq

# --- Gate / lint configs (can DISABLE a check) ---
/.pre-commit-config.yaml       @lexijamesesq
/.gitleaks.toml                @lexijamesesq

# --- Governance & policy ---
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @lexijamesesq

# --- Command-execution / trust-boundary surfaces (host command exec + root include) ---
/shell_command.yaml            @lexijamesesq
/rest_command.yaml             @lexijamesesq
/configuration.yaml            @lexijamesesq
/pyscript/                     @lexijamesesq

# UNOWNED by default (flow without the operator): the declarative HA content —
# automations.yaml, scripts.yaml, scene.yaml, sensor.yaml, binary_sensor.yaml,
# input_*.yaml, customize.yaml, group.yaml, media_player.yaml, ui-dashboard.yaml,
# fakesecrets.yaml (fixture), .storage/**, .cache/**, README.md, LICENSE.
#
# ACCEPTED RESIDUAL (surfaced, not covered): an unowned automations.yaml /
# scripts.yaml entry can invoke an existing owned shell_command with
# attacker-controlled template params without touching an owned file. Owning all
# of automations.yaml would gut the HA flow lane, so this residual is accepted.
